    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d245">

                <pb facs="0249" n="242" sameAs="frus:frus1937v03/pg242"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.3394/265: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Grew</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-07-22T17:00:00+09:00">July 22, 1937—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received July 22—5 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>221. Department’s 121, July 20, 8 p.m.<anchor n="66" xml:id="d245-f1"/></p>
                <p>The Embassy has just been orally informed by the Foreign Office that there is no
                    objection to the visit of the U. S. S. <hi rendition="#italic">Augusta</hi> and
                    accompanying vessels on the proposed dates.<anchor n="67" xml:id="d245-f2"/> The
                    Japanese Government however requests that these vessels do not enter the Inland
                    Sea <pb facs="0250" n="243" xml:id="pg243"/> during the month of September. They
                    may do so in October after the Kobe visit.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d245-f1" n="66" xml:id="d245-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d245-f2" n="67" xml:id="d245-f2-content">
                <p>September 20–October 8 to Yokohama and Kobe.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
